// AES-256-GCM envelope carrying a complete OAuth credential set (D3, §5.5):
// accessToken + refreshToken + expiresAt + full scopes + account/org metadata.
//
// Plaintext is the credential-set JSON exactly as `claude login` would produce,
// so the receiving box's Claude Code cannot distinguish it from a real login.
//
// Key: the KEK is handed to AMA by SessionSetup and held in memory only
// (§6.2, open item O1) — an off-box copy of the manifest cannot be decrypted.
// `key_id` selects which delivered KEK to use.
//
// AAD binding (§6.2): the additional authenticated data is the canonical
// concatenation of (ams_account_id, agent_id) of the intended recipient. This
// prevents a record from being copied or swapped into another agent's manifest:
// decryption on the wrong agent fails authentication rather than yielding data.
//
// ⚠ The aad_* fields below are for COMPARISON ONLY. AMA MUST construct the AAD
// from values it already holds — its own agent_id, and the ams_account_id of the
// command being processed — and MUST NOT feed these received field values into
// the AEAD. Using the attacker-supplied copy as AAD would let a relocated record
// authenticate anywhere, defeating the binding. Treat a mismatch between the
// received aad_* values and the locally derived ones as a rejected command.
//
